// flashcard drill — JAH Painter Trade Database — What painters do (jahdb demo program)
var ITEMS=[["What painters do","Painters prepare and coat surfaces: interiors, exteriors, cabinets, and specialty finishes. Prep is 80 percent of a great paint job \u2014 the painting itself is the easy part. Low startup cost makes it a classic first trade "], ["Essential tools","Quality brushes (angled sash for trim), rollers and covers, extension poles, 5-in-1 tool, putty knives, sanding sponges, painter's tape, drop cloths, and ladders. Pros add: airless sprayer and a pressure washer for exter"], ["Key skills","Surface prep: patching, sanding, caulking, priming. Cutting in clean lines. Rolling without lap marks. Spraying evenly. Color consulting with customers. Estimating accurately \u2014 measure twice, bid once."], ["Safety essentials","Ladder safety: 4-to-1 angle, three points of contact. Ventilate with oil paints and solvents. Lead paint: test pre-1978 homes, follow RRP rules. Respirators for spraying. Dispose of oily rags safely \u2014 spontaneous combust"], ["Getting started","Start as a helper learning prep; speed and neatness get you promoted. Many painters go solo within a couple of years. Get insured, build a portfolio of before/afters, and let referrals compound."], ["Pro tips","Buy the best paint the customer will pay for \u2014 it covers better and lasts longer. Back-roll sprayed exteriors for adhesion. Keep a wet edge. Box (mix) gallons for color consistency. Touch-up kits for every job earn callb"], ["Cutting in","Trade term \u2014 Cutting in: Brushing edges and corners before rolling."], ["Back-rolling","Trade term \u2014 Back-rolling: Rolling over sprayed paint for adhesion."], ["Lap mark","Trade term \u2014 Lap mark: Visible overlap lines from poor rolling technique."], ["Orange peel","Trade term \u2014 Orange peel: Textured finish from spraying or rolling."], ["Flashing","Trade term \u2014 Flashing: Uneven sheen from spot-priming or poor coverage."], ["Boxing","Trade term \u2014 Boxing: Mixing paint gallons together for color consistency."], ["